  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1153 AM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nExpect progressively hotter conditions each day this week, \nespecially on Thursday. There is a medium chance (50%) Nashville's \ntemperature could reach 100 degrees on Thursday afternoon. As such, \nthis Heat Advisory continues through Friday evening. The Cumberland \nPlateau is currently not included but will keep an eye on heat index \nobservations each day and make expansions as needed.\n\nLong range ensemble forecasts suggest this upper level ridge will \nretrograde back over to the Central Plains some time over the \nweekend, providing us with a little relief in the form of northwest \nflow aloft. This is only a brief intermission from oppressive heat, \nas this same ridging pattern sets right back in mid next week. We're \nlooking at a high chance (80-90%) of above average temperatures \nthrough the end of next week for all of Middle TN.",
